  "scope": "Ordinary pending registration and exact dispatch replay/conflict policy, retaining native admission, bounded input encoding, record/capacity/quota observations, storage, watermark reconciliation and consuming transactions.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen orchestration and its frozen dispatch comparison share native admission/codecs/storage, scheduler primitives and watermark reconciliation, not the migrated registration policy.",
    "Memory does no work without a request; exact existing requests bypass capacity regardless of dispatch phase and do not reset lease/terminal fields. Public import/adoption owns live replay behavior.",
    "Durable existing rows must be pending with identical encoded images. Bare replay skips dispatch lookup; full replay preserves native history checks, bounded request decoding and exact comparison. No missing dispatch is repaired or granted authority.",
    "Fresh bare images skip dispatch capacity/insertion only. Replay still reconciles watermarks but skips record/capacity/quota gates. Native input validation and encoding precede transaction opening.",
    "SQLite parity covers three representative operation envelopes, each with 32 scenarios and both bare/full input shapes, not all 70 durable operation combinations.",
    "Disposable corrupt fixtures restore constraints before production calls. Raw filler rows exercise the record ceiling; a view supplies a virtual oversized payload for the quota gate. These are not admitted recovery checkpoints or physical disk-full experiments.",
    "Direct hooks model exact fault/unwind and uncertain commit propagation; native triggers and deferred constraints exercise rollback. No power-loss experiment is claimed.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, standalone exported-source execution, complete host-neutral durable recovery or throughput benchmark is claimed."
  ],
